      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version of the email:\n\nSubject: Project Scope and Resource Management Concerns\n\nDear [Boss's Name],\n\nI wanted to bring to your attention some pressing concerns regarding the cloud migration project. The increasing scope and complexity have resulted in a steady stream of additional requirements that have continually slowed our progress, making it increasingly challenging to hit our original milestones without risking the stability of the entire system.\n\nAs you're aware, changes in requirements often emerge late in the sprint planning process, which not only disrupts our own workflow but also makes it difficult to communicate and agree upon new project scope. We've been struggling to filter out non-essential tasks, and the last few iterations have seen a significant increase in \"must-haves\" that were either unclear or expected. With our current team size and resource constraints, it's becoming increasingly difficult to deliver high-quality results without compromising on other critical aspects of the project.\n\nGiven these challenges, I believe it's essential to discuss possible options for expanding our team or re-evaluating the deadline to ensure we can deliver a high-quality outcome. I'd also recommend that we revisit our change management processes to minimize the occurrence of last-minute changes and ensure that all impacted stakeholders are properly informed.\n\nI'd appreciate the",
      "source": "target",
